<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    What a scuffle leaves behind (RimWorld: ThoughtDefOf.HadCatharticFight / HadAngeringFight, handed out
    50/50 by MentalState_SocialFighting.PostEnd). Their own file rather than an addition to
    Thoughts_Memories.xml, per CLAUDE.md.

    These were missing, and their absence is half of why brawling fed itself in this port: a social fight
    could only ever cost mood - Insulted on the way in, pain and witnessed injuries on the way out - and
    never clear the air. In RimWorld half of all fights end with both parties feeling BETTER than before.

    The mood magnitudes could not be sourced against RimWorld's own Thoughts_Memory_Social.xml from this
    environment. They are stated here as a pair whose SHAPE is what matters and is pinned by test
    (SocialTests): cathartic is positive, angering is negative, they are the same size, and both are smaller
    than the Insulted memory that started the fight - a fight is a smaller event than the grudge behind it.
    The opinion offsets follow the same shape: a fight you got something out of thaws a relationship
    slightly, one that only made you angrier chills it.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>HadCatharticFight</defName>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.5</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>2</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>cathartic fight</label>
        <description>We had it out. I feel better for it.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>4</baseMoodEffect>
        <baseOpinionOffset>5</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>HadAngeringFight</defName>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.5</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>2</stackLimitForSameOtherPawn>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>angering fight</label>
        <description>We came to blows and it settled nothing.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-4</baseMoodEffect>
        <baseOpinionOffset>-5</baseOpinionOffset>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
